
# Interview Query 

1) To N ( Top 3 Salaries at each dfepartment)

- 2 table 1) Employee  2)Department

WITH RankedSalaries AS (
    SELECT 
        e.name,
        d.department_name,
        e.salary,
        DENSE_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY e.department_id ORDER BY e.salary DESC) AS salary_rank
    FROM 
        employee e
    JOIN 
        department d ON e.department_id = d.department_id
)
SELECT 
    department_name,
    name,
    salary
FROM 
    RankedSalaries
WHERE 
    salary_rank <= 3
ORDER BY 
    department_name ASC, 
    salary DESC, 
    name ASC;

# Rownumber -  You want to select the single highest-paid employee in each department.
ROW_NUMBER() ensures only one employee is selected, even if others have the same salary.

# Rank- You want to identify the top 3 salaries in each department, 
but it's acceptable if there are gaps in the rank numbers.

# DenseRank - You want to identify the top 3 salaries in each department, ensuring no rank numbers are skipped.


